{"text": "And today your ladder is in its third fight — this one still open. Two teams, two numbers for how fast the universe grows. One number comes from the oldest light there is. A satellite called plahnk reads sixty-seven point four, with an error of half a point. The other comes off your ladder. Parallax, to SEF-ee-ids, to exploding stars that all flare to nearly the same true brightness. The ladder team, called shoes, reads seventy-three point oh, plus or minus one. A five-sigma difference, in their own words: far too large to be chance. You'll hear that sold as the early universe against today's. Watch what that framing skips. A second team climbed the same ladder with a different second rung. Red giant stars instead of SEF-ee-ids, the new James Webb telescope in the mix. They read sixty-seven point eight to seventy point four, depending on the sample and the method. Their own verdict: no new physics needed. Strangest of all: both teams agree on the distances to the very same galaxies. To about one percent. The stars are not the quarrel. The quarrel is over which exploding stars to hang the scale on. The ladder holds. The fight is about the nail. Nobody yet knows which side is right.", "alignment": {"characters": ["A", "n", "d", " ", "t", "o", "d", "a", "y", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "l", "a", "d", "d", "e", "r", " ", "i", "s", " ", "i", "n", " ", "i", "t", "s", " ", "t", "h", "i", "r", "d", " ", "f", "i", "g", "h", "t", " ", "—", " ", "t", "h", "i", "s", " ", "o", "n", "e", " ", "s", "t", "i", "l", "l", " ", "o", "p", "e", "n", ".", " ", "T", "w", "o", " ", "t", "e", "a", "m", "s", ",", " ", "t", "w", "o", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", "s", " ", "f", "o", "r", " ", "h", "o", "w", " ", "f", "a", "s", "t", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "u", "n", "i", "v", "e", "r", "s", "e", " ", "g", "r", "o", "w", "s", ".", " ", "O", "n", "e", " ", "n", "u", "m", "b", "e", "r", " ", "c", "o", "m", "e", "s", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "o", "l", "d",